### TEMPLATE_RAW_NAME — try the API (Visual Studio, Rider or the VS Code REST Client extension)
### 1. Start the API:   dotnet run --project src/TEMPLATE_RAW_NAME.Api
### 2. Create a token:  dotnet user-jwts create --project src/TEMPLATE_RAW_NAME.Api
###    and paste it below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@token = paste-the-token-from-dotnet-user-jwts-here
@customerId = 0199f0a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001

### Health (no token needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Place an order (A-1 has 100 in stock, B-2 has 5)
# @name placeOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "A-1", "quantity": 2 },
    { "sku": "B-2", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Not enough stock: 409, nothing is saved and OrderPlaced is not dispatched
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "lines": [{ "sku": "B-2", "quantity": 50 }]
}

### Get the order
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List orders (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?index=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cancel the order (soft delete: the order and its lines)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cancelled orders are hidden...
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ...unless you ask for them
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}?includeDeleted=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
